<!doctype html><html lang="zh-CN"><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><title>Gray/Contour model-list renderer evidence and proposed boundary</title><style>body{margin:0;background:#101a29;color:#e7edf7;font:16px/1.8 "Microsoft YaHei",sans-serif}main{max-width:1150px;margin:auto;padding:24px}a{color:#9fd5ff}nav{position:sticky;top:0;background:#172638;padding:12px;z-index:2;display:flex;gap:22px;flex-wrap:wrap}pre{overflow:auto;background:#09131f;padding:16px}code{font:13px/1.7 Consolas,monospace}table{border-collapse:collapse;display:block;overflow:auto}td,th{border:1px solid #45617e;padding:8px 12px}blockquote{border-left:4px solid #e7b667;margin:18px 0;padding:1px 16px;background:#203249}h1,h2,h3,h4{scroll-margin-top:85px}img{max-width:100%}.meta{font-size:12px;color:#a9bfd3;overflow-wrap:anywhere}summary{cursor:pointer}</style><nav><a href="../../../framework-architecture.html">主架构</a><a href="../../main-ui-map.html">逆向核心</a><a href="../index.html">关联文档目录</a><a data-source-download download href="../../../plugins/GRAY-MATCH-SHARED-MODEL-RENDERER-CONTRACT.md">下载原始文件</a></nav><main><h1 id="graycontour-model-list-renderer-evidence-and-proposed-boundary">Gray/Contour model-list renderer evidence and proposed boundary</h1><p>Original Gray <code>Apps.XmlParser.ParamTab.GrayMatchVAConfigPanalData</code> and Contour <code>PyramidFeaturepatMatchConfigPanalData</code> both inherit <code>FeaturepatMatchConfigPanalData</code>. Their <code>DisplayType</code> getter is exactly <code>((object)this).GetType().BaseType.Name</code>, with an empty setter. Both therefore resolve to <code>FeaturepatMatchConfigPanalData</code>. Original files are under the matching <code>IMVSGrayMatchModuVAControl</code> and <code>IMVSContourMatchModuControl</code> directories in <code>analysis/full-audit/renderer-gap-projects</code>. This supports one shared renderer, not shared training or file formats: Gray overrides <code>.gmvaxml</code>, <code>GrayMatchVADialogData</code> and <code>GrayMatchVADialogUI</code>; Contour overrides <code>.contourmxml</code> and its pyramid-specific dialog/data.</p>
<p>Current <code>src/VisionPlugins.ContourMatch/ContourModelControls.cs</code> directly captures <code>ContourModelCollection</code>, reads <code>Storage.Snapshot</code>, and calls Select/Rename/Move/Delete/Clear. The renderer never reads the model&#39;s binary Data. Minimal proposed injected backend:</p>
<pre><code class="language-csharp">record ModelListItem(int Index, byte[] RawName, bool Selected);
interface IModelListBackend {
    IReadOnlyList&lt;ModelListItem&gt; Snapshot();
    uint Select(int index, bool selected);
    uint Rename(int index, byte[] utf8Name);
    uint Move(int index, bool up);
    uint Delete(int index);
    void Clear();
}
</code></pre>
<p>This is an independent transport contract, not an original SDK ABI. Snapshot bytes must be owned copies. Each adapter owns its native-equivalent mutation, model sidecar operations and persistence callback; the renderer must not persist a second time. Contour currently persists within collection Move/Delete/Clear, but separately after Storage.Select/Rename. An adapter normalizes that call boundary while retaining actual failure/partial-commit behavior; it must not invent transaction rollback. Gray uses its own model state and training actions. Training, load and edit remain separate injected <code>Action build</code>, <code>Action load</code>, <code>Action&lt;int&gt; edit</code>; running predicate, confirmation, notification/localization and operation-error caption are injected too. No <code>Contour</code> label or concrete storage type belongs in shared code.</p>
<p>Original <code>FeatureMatchCommonControl.ModelItem.ModelNameTextChangedCommandExcute</code> checks TextBox input and text length &gt;32, selects <code>ChooseSpareModelIndex = Id-1</code>, then checks whitespace and writes UTF8 <code>ChangeSpareModelName</code>. It has no running guard in this method. Consequently the current Contour rename handler&#39;s absence of <code>Run</code> wrapper must not be accidentally changed while extracting the renderer. Its current whitespace-before-select implementation is not proof of original selection side effects. Button and selection running guards are separate original paths. The existing TextBox MaxLength63 and rename limit32 are distinct; do not collapse them based on intent.</p>
<p>This report proposes the smallest shared extraction only. Root owns shared implementation and Contour adaptation. Gray model slots, training and file payload remain D-owned; successful model-slot arithmetic checks do not complete training/search, original file interoperability or full plugin execution.</p>
